The diff changes the years case in `parse` from `return n * y` to `return n / y`. Since `y` is the number of milliseconds in a year (86400000 × 365.25 = 31557600000), parsing a duration in years must *multiply* to convert to milliseconds. With the patch, `ms('2y')` returns 2 / 31557600000 ≈ 6.3e-11 instead of 63115200000 — an obvious behavioural break (the library's own suite simply doesn't exercise year parsing).

```json
